# Pipeline script rules

## 02_preprocess.py
- Any new historical/aggregate feature must be built with
  `expanding_prior_dist` / `expanding_prior_rate` (or the same
  cumsum-minus-current-row pattern). Full-dataset aggregates are only
  allowed for the inference artifacts (`pitcher_priors`, arsenal mask,
  matchup table, batter profiles) and the arsenal mask — never as model
  features.
- Do not reorder rows after the chronological sort.
- `build_sequences` groups by `(game_pk, pitcher)`; keep the same-at-bat
  flag as the last timestep feature.
- If you change the feature layout, update `meta_v5.json` keys
  (`seq_feats`, `ctx_feats`, `ctx_feature_names`, `pitch_classes`) — the
  training script reads shapes from there, and the website will too.
- Keep `data_v5/` and `_v5` artifact names; `run_pipeline.sh/.bat` check
  `data_v5/meta_v5.json` to decide whether to skip preprocessing.

## 03_train.py
- The arsenal mask input must stay wired to the logits
  (`logits + (1 - mask) * -1e9` before softmax). Removing it silently
  reintroduces impossible predictions.
- No `RandomOverSampler` / row duplication. Class balance is the
  per-class alpha vector in `focal_loss`.
- `train_test_split` on natural indices first; all evaluation on
  `idx_val`.
- Keep the printed evaluation block intact (top-1, top-3, baseline,
  report, confusion matrix) — those are what get pasted back and logged.
- Change ONE hyperparameter/architecture item per run.

## 01_scrape_statcast.py
- Write outputs to a temp path and `os.replace` into place.
- Exit non-zero on failure paths (the runners rely on the exit code).
- Adding a Statcast column: add it to `KEEP_COLUMNS`; downstream code
  must tolerate its absence (older scrapes).
